  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 303 AM MDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nWill have slightly cooler conditions today but still warm with\nhighs in the 60s mountains and 70s valleys. Upper ridge builds\nin Sunday with very warm conditions Sunday through Wednesday.\nHighs tomorrow into the 80s low elevations and 60s and 70s\nmountains. By Tuesday many low elevations will reach the lower\n90s. And even some mountain areas will hit the 80s. It will be\nthe warmest day of spring so far. No precipiation is expected\nthrough Tuesday. Ridge moves east Wednesday and southerly flow\naloft increases which should return some moisture and allow at\nleast a slight chance of showers and thunderstorms late\nWednesday into next Saturday.",
